sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant API as Chat API and session lease
    participant T as GameTurnManager
    participant W as Technical model and domain validators
    participant NPC as Optional NPC Personality
    participant N as Narration model
    participant DB as Canonical session state
    participant BG as Deferred memory and visual work

    Note over C,BG: Main foreground paths. Commands, combat, terminal reports and prose-only regeneration have separate branches.
    C->>API: Submit a session chat request
    API->>T: Process under the existing mutation/recovery boundary
    T->>DB: Load scoped state, history and settings
    alt RPG or Story mechanics
        T->>W: Propose mechanics and resolve host rule checks
        W-->>T: Accepted outcomes and denied actions
    else Visual Novel
        T->>W: Propose VN progression, movement and access
        W-->>T: Validated world outcomes
    else Chat
        Note over T,W: Applicable host rules and optional generator tools still apply
    end
    T-->>C: Status and intermediate state events
    opt NPC Personality enabled or observed
        T->>NPC: Prepare observer-scoped context and bounded decisions
        opt Existing tool rounds enabled
            NPC->>DB: Read accessible evidence and current state by exact ID
            DB-->>NPC: Bounded source-bound observations
        end
        NPC-->>T: Plans or observation-only results, according to mode
    end
    T->>N: Narrate host outcomes and applicable accepted NPC plans
    loop Narration chunks
        N-->>T: Candidate prose chunk
        alt Ordinary unbuffered narration
            T-->>C: Prose chunk before reconciliation and commit
        else Live CHPM buffered decisions or simplified review
            Note over T,C: Retain prose on the server until review and commit
        end
    end
    opt Live NPC shared review
        T->>NPC: Validate shared narration meaning and grounded effects
        NPC-->>T: Accept, bounded repair or existing fallback/error policy
    end
    opt Completed VN narration
        T->>W: Reconcile supported item, clothing and condition facts
        W-->>T: Independently validated deltas and rejection diagnostics
        Note over T,W: Optional scene staging retains its separate reconciliation boundary
    end
    T->>DB: Persist reply, source bindings, canonical changes and selected visual moment
    T->>DB: Commit the completed turn
    T-->>BG: Schedule eligible journal, recall and visual maintenance
    opt Live CHPM buffered delivery
        T-->>C: Reviewed prose after reconciliation and commit
    end
    T-->>C: Final receipt or explicit incomplete/error outcome
    Note over C,BG: Speech and image rendering use their own settings. Neither authorizes a world-state mutation.
